<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>\mathbf{a} = {-5 \mathbf{i}+6 \mathbf{j}-6 \mathbf{k}}</m> and <m>\mathbf{b} = {-6 \mathbf{i}-3 \mathbf{j}-4 \mathbf{k}}</m>.</p><p>(a) Find <m>\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}</m> as a column vector.</p><div><m>\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>{4}\mathbf{a} + {4}\mathbf{b}</m> in i, j, k form.</p><div><m>{4}\mathbf{a} + {4}\mathbf{b} =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Work component by component.</p><p>(a) <m>\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -5 \\ 6 \\ -6 \end{array}\right)} - {\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -3 \\ -4 \end{array}\right)} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 1 \\ 9 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(b) A scalar multiplies every component; it never adds to them. <m>{4}\mathbf{a} = {-20 \mathbf{i}+24 \mathbf{j}-24 \mathbf{k}}</m> and <m>{4}\mathbf{b} = {-24 \mathbf{i}-12 \mathbf{j}-16 \mathbf{k}}</m>, so <m>{4}\mathbf{a} + {4}\mathbf{b} = {-44 \mathbf{i}+12 \mathbf{j}-40 \mathbf{k}}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 1 \\ 9 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-44 \mathbf{i}+12 \mathbf{j}-40 \mathbf{k}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>